# Frontend build-time configuration.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      then edit, then `npm run build` (or docker build)
#
# Leave VITE_API_BASE_URL UNSET for the default same-origin deployment, where
# nginx (or the Vite dev proxy) reverse-proxies /api and /ws to the backend on
# the same host:port the browser loaded the page from.
#
# Set it when the frontend is built to be served standalone (its own static
# host/CDN/nginx with NO reverse proxy to the backend) and must call a backend
# running on a different host or port — e.g. a separate VM, a different port,
# or a different domain entirely.
#
# IMPORTANT: Vite bakes VITE_-prefixed variables into the compiled JS at BUILD
# time, not at container start. Set this before `npm run build` /
# `docker build`; changing it afterward requires rebuilding.
#
# Examples:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.50:8000
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# If VITE_API_BASE_URL is set to a different origin than the frontend, add
# that frontend's origin to the backend's CORS_ORIGINS (backend/.env), e.g.:
#   CORS_ORIGINS=["http://192.168.1.50:8080"]
# so the browser is allowed to call it and the auth cookie is accepted.
